Restore the containment check in both commands, and prefer `filepath.Clean`/`filepath.Rel` over a string prefix test so that sibling directories such as `/etc/uniget-evil` do not pass:

    hookFileAbs, err := filepath.Abs(hookFile)
    if err != nil { return err }
    hooksDirAbs, err := filepath.Abs(hooksDir)
    if err != nil { return err }
    rel, err := filepath.Rel(hooksDirAbs, hookFileAbs)
    if err != nil || rel == ".." || strings.HasPrefix(rel, ".."+string(os.PathSeparator)) {
        return fmt.Errorf("hook file %s is outside of hookDir %s", hookFile, hooksDir)
    }

Better still, reject the argument up front unless it is a bare filename (`filepath.Base(args[0]) == args[0]`), matching what `addHooksCmd` already does by taking only the last path segment of `--source`. Separately, if the symlink protection in `processHooks` and `editHooksCmd` is still wanted, reimplement it correctly — `fi, err := os.Lstat(p); err == nil && fi.Mode()&os.ModeSymlink != 0` — rather than deleting it.
